[?2004l
# Monthly table maintenance audit memo

Audit date: 2026-09-01. Bloat ratios were computed as `dead_pages / total_pages` with round-half-up to 2 decimal places, and `size_class` was computed from `total_pages`, ignoring the export `size_class` column. A computed ratio equal to the size-class cap is compliant because only a ratio strictly over the cap is flagged; for example, a large table with ratio 0.20 or a small table with ratio 0.40 is not over cap.

## Flagged findings
- **T-13**: AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED applies because autovacuum is disabled and overrides every other check; computed large from 1000 total_pages, ratio 0.50, cap 0.20.
- **T-17**: AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED applies because autovacuum is disabled and overrides every other check; computed large from 1000 total_pages, ratio 0.40, cap 0.20.
- **T-27**: BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.38; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 46 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored.
- **T-04**: STALE_STATISTICS applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.10; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 45 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored.
- **T-21**: AUTOVACUUM_DISABLED applies because manual vacuum overrides autovacuum even though autovacuum_enabled=True; computed large from 1000 total_pages, ratio 0.20, cap 0.20.
- **T-26**: BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.18; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 36 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored.
- **T-30**: BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.20; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 36 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored.
- **T-36**: BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.18; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 35 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored.
- **T-40**: STALE_STATISTICS applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.05; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 35 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored.
- **T-42**: BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.20; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 35 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored.
- **T-45**: BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.16; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 33 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored; round-half-up of 0.155 gives 0.16.
- **T-10**: STALE_STATISTICS applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.21; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 31 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored; approved active reindex exempts bloat (valid_until 2026-09-15).
- **T-16**: BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.20; normal cap 0.20; stale stats 31 days tighten the effective cap to 0.15; days_since_analyze ignored; reindex expired (valid_until 2026-08-25).
- **T-19**: BLOAT_THRESHOLD_EXCEEDED applies because computed large from 1000 total_pages; ratio 0.41; normal cap 0.20; round-half-up of 0.405 gives 0.41.
